The Na'at Keystone License
Version 1.0

  na'at (Yucatec Maya): to understand, to solve, to figure the thing out.
  keystone: the stone at the crown of an arch that locks every other stone
  in place; remove it and the arch falls.

  Intelligence is the keystone. Understanding is the craft. This license
  keeps both in the commons.

Copyright (c) 2026 Hue. Every freedom not withheld below is granted below.


PREAMBLE

A license for builders, learners, workers, artists, researchers, small teams,
independent labs, and companies who believe intelligence should remain a
practice people can touch.

This work is released for the new era of making.

You are free to use it, study it, change it, train with it, build from it,
self-host it, teach with it, ship with it, and sell what you create with it.

You may build products, tools, models, agents, interfaces, research systems,
education systems, and infrastructure from this work.

The only covenant is fairness:

Give credit.
Preserve provenance.
Do not erase the commons.
Do not pretend shared work was born closed.
Do not use openness as a ladder and then pull the ladder away.

Artificial intelligence is not a priesthood.
It is a trade.
It is a craft.
It is a public instrument.

This license exists so that people can learn the machine, shape the machine,
question the machine, and build with the machine without asking permission
from a permanent ruling class.

Build freely.
Attribute honestly.
Return improvements to the shared core when you offer the core back to the
world as a service.
Protect the user's agency.
Keep the craft alive.

The Preamble above states the intent of this license. The Terms below give it
force. Where the Terms are silent, read them in the spirit of the Preamble.


